# Orchestration runtime (managed by set-core).
#
# Ignored means `git clean -fdx` deletes it and a fresh clone never has it. Most of
# what lives here is genuinely ephemeral (loop state, telemetry journals — the
# resolver runs cold on absence), but two are not: `.set/issues/registry.json` holds
# the issue registry, and `.set/reflection.md` is the agent learning file. Neither is
# recoverable from git, because this rule is why git never saw them.
#
# Track them deliberately if that history matters to you — they will then contain
# whatever your issues contain, which is a decision about your repository, not one
# set-core should make for you.
/.set/

# Orchestration runtime journals (written at project root by dispatcher/merger)
journals/
orchestration-events-*.jsonl
set/orchestration/activity-detail-*.jsonl
set/orchestration/spec-coverage-history.jsonl
set/orchestration/e2e-manifest-history.jsonl

